{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1072485-corpse-mutilation-in-england","id":1072485,"title":"Corpse Mutilation in England","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-03T06:25:37-07:00","id":1072485,"title":"Corpse Mutilation in England","content":"Fun new article in the Guardian today about a geological dig showing non-cannibalistic post-mortem mutilation of corpses, presumably as a ritualistic way to prevent the dead from rising again. I can't link to it (forum rules and all), but I'll highlight the key points. <br /> <br /> The finds date between the 11th and 14th centuries in the town of Wharram Percy, a well-preserved abandoned village in Yorkshire. There were 137 bone fragments, from at least 10 different bodies, all of which showed cut marks not consistent with butchering, and all of whom were locals based on their teeth isotopes, so not a massacre of outsiders either. 7 were adults, 2 were women, the youngest was 2 and the oldest 50. They were not buried in the graveyard, but in overlapping pits between the houses. Specifically, they were decapitated. <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Simon Mays, skeletal biologist at Historic England, said: \u201cThe idea that the Wharram Percy bones are the remains of corpses burnt and dismembered to stop them walking from their graves seems to fit the evidence best. If we are right, then this is the first good archaeological evidence we have for this practice.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">He added: \u201cIt shows us a dark side of medieval beliefs and provides a graphic reminder of how different the medieval view of the world was from our own.\u201d<br /> <br /> So, did the medieval villagers of Wharram Percy catch a coterie of Kindred? Did an outsider Kindred direct the villagers to his enemies? How many of the deceased truly were vampires? Or were any? Did the true vampire escape the purge? <br /> <br /> I love little things I can drop references to in my game, and this'll definitely make it in at some point. </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T07:18:38-07:00","id":1072513,"title":"","content":"I'd say none of the dead were Kindred at all. If I was running that scenario, I'd say that a local vampire wasn't careful with repeated feeding from a weakened (possibly plague-ridden) vessel and the one victim rose as a Revenant, went on a little bit of a rampage their first night, and was summarily defeated. But once you've seen one Revenant arise from the corpse of someone who died (to your knowledge) of plague or tuberculosis, wouldn't you want to dismember and burn <i>every </i>corpse of a person who died of plague or tuberculosis, just in case?<br /> <br /> It's a complication for local Kindred, not a direct assault. The villagers are on high alert because one idiot allowed a Masquerade breach, and now they're watching the cemeteries and looking suspiciously at strangers who come out at night. Who is one of the Hungry Dead? Who isn't? What folk remedies for plague, tuberculosis, or vampirism, will they try in an effort to protect themselves? If anyone in the village has ancestors from places where vampire folklore is more prevalent, like Eastern Europe, do they start to look suspiciously at redheads, because supposedly they are destined to become vampires in death? Was it a Masquerade breach at all, or was one of the Strix taking the corpse for a joy ride, and is now sitting back and watching the turmoil with glee?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}